{% comment %}
  B1 (GOAL_SCORECARD.md, session 4): gwern-style hover link previews --
  re-implemented from scratch (interaction pattern only; the standing project
  convention -- see DECISIONS.md's olah_blog entry -- is re-implement rather
  than copy, applied here too even though gwern.net itself states most of its
  own content is public-domain/CC0). No live fetch, no third-party service:
  builds a {url: {title, description}} map at Jekyll BUILD time from every
  real page/post/project/news item's own front matter, and hands it to
  assets/js/hover-previews.js, which shows a small popup card when the mouse
  hovers a link matching a known internal URL. External links are left alone
  -- this site has no metadata to preview them with, and fetching a live
  oEmbed/screenshot for arbitrary external URLs is a materially bigger,
  separate piece of work, not silently folded in here.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign preview_items = '' | split: '' %}
{% for item in site.pages %}
  {% if item.title and item.url != '/' %}{% assign preview_items = preview_items | push: item %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% for item in site.posts -%}
  {%- if item.title %}{% assign preview_items = preview_items | push: item %}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor %}
{% for item in site.projects -%}
  {%- if item.title %}{% assign preview_items = preview_items | push: item %}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor %}
{% for item in site.news -%}
  {%- if item.title %}{% assign preview_items = preview_items | push: item %}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor %}
<script>
  window.__hoverPreviews = {
    {% for item in preview_items %}
      {{ item.url | relative_url | jsonify }}: {
        title: {{ item.title | strip_html | jsonify }},
        description: {{ item.description | default: "" | strip_html | jsonify }}
      }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {% endfor %}
  };
</script>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/hover-previews.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
